  "findings": [
    "The SDK sender-info shareHandle is uint32_t. Native observations accept only its zero/sign-extended representations; native access handles stay unchanged.",
    "SDK copy-counter joins alone do not establish which producer images reached the consumer. GPU marker words independently expose the disagreement.",
    "Q01 sample: all 180 accepted output versions are captured; 141 disagree with exact renderer source-use labels and only 39 match both source cards.",
    "Q02 sample: 144 of 180 accepted output versions are captured; 138 disagree, six match and 36 have no independent capture.",
    "Q01 whole-capture mismatches often match an earlier neighboring renderer prediction. Input-copy versus output-copy origin remains undetermined.",
    "Both samples have complete CPU source-publication-to-output-API observations. These metadata ages do not prove that the labeled pixels were delivered.",
    "Genuine native removal/bounded stuck retirement and complete renderer qualification remain open."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Short unpinned diagnostics cannot establish prescribed qualification or causal performance differences.",
    "Age distributions of the 39/six exact sample matches are incomplete subsets and cannot qualify full output age.",
    "Legacy handle/counter reuse remains ambiguous; repeated captures cannot replace a missing output image.",
    "CPU API brackets bound copy admission to capture completion; they are not GPU queue timestamps or window presentation.",
    "Separate context-local GPU spans are never summed into a critical path.",
    "Plan publication/receipt, GPU/presentation queue age, physical output, sustained growth/handles and complete recovery remain unverified."
  ],
